                        "review": "These are my thoughts about the game:\r\n\r\nFirst, I'll discuss the gameplay. It has massive improvements on everything. Puzzle variety, less trial-and-error, stealth mechanics, refined horror, and smoother progression. You progress in each chapter and these chapters reveal the story and connect the threads from the first game.\r\n\r\nThe visuals have also improved. I don't think I'll say much other than the fact that the art style and visual effects are slightly more fascinating to see compared to what the first game has offered. It truly is a stunning improvement as well.\r\n\r\nThe music evokes our emotions. It's not just there for us to hear, but feeling the music in specific moments connects us with the character. Sound effects are stellar with their ability to evoke emotions in us as players, giving you dread, fear, and any other emotions to feel.\r\n\r\n(Warning ⚠️ : It may or may not be a spoiler to you so be warned reading this part. I will be diving into the narrative and themes based on how I interpreted it, but I think the review remains safe for new players.)\r\n\r\nLastly, the story. Our discovery of Price's history and his life has showed how trauma can affect us in the long run, and ignoring it can bring us stagnation. In this game, there are things I have come to realize.\r\n\r\nOur fears, insecurities, and unworthiness would hold us back from our potential of who we can become. With reason to live, we can face our losses and regrets. Our ambitions, inspirations, and desire for comfort and love can help us confront our fears and agony.\r\n\r\nAlso, by forgiving ourselves, a spark of courage surges to pursue the things we hope for. This is how impactful the sequel is. It's an eye-opening game for all of us. This game absolutely deserves the overwhelmingly positive reviews and I highly recommend playing this game.",
